---
// Pagina di supporto di Minta. L'app la apre da Impostazioni › Info › Support
// (AppLinks.support nel progetto MintaApp): l'indirizzo app/minta/support/ non
// si cambia senza cambiare anche l'app.
//
// Ogni risposta viene dal codice dell'app o dall'informativa approvata
// (MintaApp/Documentation/INFORMATIVA-PRIVACY-BOZZA.md), verificati il
// 3 ottobre 2026 e riletti il 27 ottobre 2026 sul CHANGELOG dell'app fino al
// Lotto 75 — non da come l'app "dovrebbe" funzionare. Se l'app cambia
// (lingue, percorsi nelle Impostazioni, regole del credito), si rilegge qui.
//
// Contatto: dan@trova.me, lo stesso della pagina privacy/. Deciso dal proprietario
// il 19 ottobre 2026 (prima, dal 3 ottobre, qui non c'era nessun indirizzo):
// Apple chiede un modo di contatto nella pagina di supporto (regola 1.5).
// Dal 19 ottobre 2026 (Lotto 33 dell'app) il contatto chiede anche il codice di
// supporto (MNT-XXXX-XXXX, in Impostazioni › Minta Cloud): serve solo a trovare
// l'account nel server, non e' una credenziale.
//
// 27 ottobre 2026: le registrazioni possono stare anche nel proprio iCloud
// (Lotto 11a); la trascrizione e' solo sul telefono, con i motori nuovi di Apple,
// e non va piu' ai server di Apple (Lotto 75): il modello di una lingua lo scarica
// l'iPhone, la registrazione aspetta e si trascrive da sola quando arriva.
// Whisper resta legato al primo acquisto (WhisperOffer, has_purchased).
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { path } from '../../../lib/paths';
---

<Base
  titolo="Minta support | TROVA.ME"
  descrizione="Help with Minta: short answers about recordings, your Minta Cloud account and credit, languages and refunds."
>
  <div class="contenitore">
    <div class="testata">
      <p class="etichetta">Minta</p>
      <h1>Support</h1>
      <p class="apertura">
        Short answers to the questions people ask most about Minta. If yours isn’t here,
        write to <a href="mailto:dan@trova.me">dan@trova.me</a>.
      </p>
    </div>


    <section class="sezione">
      <h2>Common questions</h2>
      <div class="domande">
        <details class="domanda">
          <summary><h3>Where are my recordings kept?</h3></summary>
          <div class="risposta">
            <p>
              On your iPhone, and in your own iCloud if you turn on sync in Minta. Recordings,
              transcriptions and write-ups stay there until you delete them, and they can be
              included in your iPhone backups. Minta keeps no copy on a server, so I can’t bring
              back a recording you deleted. The details are on the <a href={path('privacy/')}
                >privacy page</a
              >.
            </p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="domanda">
          <summary><h3>How do I delete my Minta Cloud account? What happens to my credit?</h3></summary>
          <div class="risposta">
            <p>
              In Minta, go to Settings › Minta Cloud › Delete account, and confirm with
              Apple. Your account and its data on Minta’s server are deleted; your recordings
              stay on your iPhone.
            </p>
            <p>
              Any credit you have left is lost and can’t be recovered, and so are any free
              write-ups left from the trial: a new account doesn’t get a new free trial. If you
              only want to stop using Minta Cloud, choose Sign out instead — it keeps your
              account and credit for when you sign in again.
            </p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="domanda">
          <summary><h3>I paid, but the credit isn’t there.</h3></summary>
          <div class="risposta">
            <p>
              Once Apple has charged you, Minta adds the credit automatically, without charging
              you again. Usually it’s enough to close and reopen Minta. If it says “Sign in
              again to receive your credit”, sign in with Apple and the credit arrives on its
              own. If it still hasn’t arrived after that, write to <a href="mailto:dan@trova.me"
                >dan@trova.me</a
              > with the date of the purchase.
            </p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="domanda">
          <summary><h3>What does “Processing on the server…” mean?</h3></summary>
          <div class="risposta">
            <p>
              Your audio or text has reached Minta Cloud and the server is working on it, so it
              can no longer be stopped: it is already being paid for.
            </p>
            <p>
              If iOS interrupts Minta or the connection drops, reopen Minta once you’re online:
              it asks for the same result again, without charging you twice. The server holds
              the result in memory for up to 15 minutes for exactly this, then deletes it. If
              Minta tells you a result was lost and you were charged for it, write to <a
                href="mailto:dan@trova.me">dan@trova.me</a
              >.
            </p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="domanda">
          <summary><h3>Which languages can Minta transcribe? Does it happen on my iPhone?</h3></summary>
          <div class="risposta">
            <p>
              Sixteen languages: Arabic, Chinese, Dutch, English (US and UK), French, German,
              Hindi, Italian, Japanese, Korean, Polish, Portuguese, Russian, Spanish, Swedish
              and Turkish. Choose yours in Settings › Transcription.
            </p>
            <p>
              Yes: transcription happens only on your iPhone, with Apple’s speech recognition.
              The first time you use a language, the iPhone downloads its model from Apple,
              with none of your data. It can take a while: the recording waits, and Minta
              transcribes it on its own as soon as the model arrives. If your iPhone can’t
              transcribe a language at all, Minta tells you and offers Minta Cloud Whisper.
            </p>
            <p>
              With Minta Cloud, after your first credit purchase, you can also choose Minta
              Cloud Whisper: transcription on the server, paid from your credit, and useful in
              noisy rooms or with quiet voices. It takes recordings up to 3 hours.
            </p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="domanda">
          <summary><h3>How do I get a refund?</h3></summary>
          <div class="risposta">
            <p>
              Purchases go through Apple, and so do refunds: ask at <a
                href="https://reportaproblem.apple.com">reportaproblem.apple.com</a
              >, signed in with your Apple Account. I can’t issue refunds myself.
            </p>
          </div>
        </details>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="sezione">
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p class="contatto">
        Write to <a href="mailto:dan@trova.me">dan@trova.me</a>. I make Minta and I read every
        message myself. If you use Minta Cloud, include the support code from Settings › Minta
        Cloud: it lets me find your account. If it’s about a purchase, include its date.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .testata {
    padding: 48px 0 0;
  }

  .testata h1 {
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }


  /* Domande richiuse: da telefono si vede subito l'elenco, e si apre solo
     quella che serve. <details> e' HTML puro, nessun JavaScript. */
  .domande {
    max-width: var(--lettura);
    margin-top: 4px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--bordo);
  }

  .domanda {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--bordo);
  }

  .domanda summary {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 16px;
    padding: 18px 0;
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .domanda summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  .domanda summary::after {
    content: '+';
    flex: none;
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    line-height: 1;
    color: var(--accento);
  }

  .domanda[open] summary::after {
    content: '−';
  }

  .domanda h3 {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .risposta {
    padding-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .risposta p {
    margin: 0 0 10px;
    color: var(--tenue);
  }

  .risposta p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .contatto {
    max-width: var(--lettura);
    margin: 0;
  }

  @media (min-width: 48rem) {
    .testata {
      padding-top: 72px;
    }
  }
</style>
